EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

This report documents a security assessment performed against the web application hosted at https://luxoralk.vercel.app/ ("LUXORA"), carried out by the author as the site's own developer/owner for the purpose of a university security project. The objective was to evaluate the application's exposure to common web application vulnerabilities, following a methodology aligned with the OWASP Testing Guide and OWASP Top 10.

This document is provided as a structured assessment template and working report. Sections 5 and 6 contain checklists that should be completed by executing the listed tools/tests against the target and recording the observed results, since live scanning requires tools (browser, Burp Suite / OWASP ZAP, SSL Labs, securityheaders.com, nmap) run from the tester's own machine or lab environment.

Note on scope: because this is a lightweight, statically-hosted Vercel deployment, testing was restricted to non-destructive, passive/black-box techniques (reconnaissance, header analysis, configuration review). No exploitation, denial-of-service, brute-force, or destructive testing was performed or is recommended without additional written authorization.

