METHODOLOGY

The assessment follows the general phases recommended by the OWASP Web Security Testing Guide (WSTG):

Reconnaissance & Information Gathering – identify technology stack, hosting, exposed metadata
Mapping the Application – enumerate pages, routes, forms, and client-side assets
Configuration & Deployment Management Testing – HTTP headers, TLS/SSL configuration, exposed files
Identity, Authentication & Session Management Testing – if the app has login/session features
Input Validation Testing – XSS, injection points in forms/query parameters
Client-Side Testing – DOM XSS, exposed JavaScript source maps, hard-coded secrets
Reporting – documenting findings, severity, and remediation guidance
