GENERAL RECOMMENDATIONS

Based on the findings in Section 7, the following steps are recommended, in priority order:

PRIORITY 1 – Add the missing security headers via next.config.js (async headers()) or a vercel.json headers block: Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options (or CSP frame-ancestors), X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy, and Permissions-Policy
PRIORITY 2 – Restrict Access-Control-Allow-Origin to specific trusted origins instead of "*", unless this route is intentionally a public CDN asset
Disable source map generation for production builds unless required, or restrict access to them
Store all secrets/API keys as Vercel environment variables, never in client-side code
Validate and sanitize all user input on both client and server (API routes)
Enable Vercel's built-in DDoS/bot protection and consider a Web Application Firewall for public launch
Keep Next.js, React and all npm dependencies patched (npm audit / Dependabot)
Restrict CORS on any API routes to known origins only
Review cookies/session tokens for Secure, HttpOnly and SameSite attributes
